<div class="title">Student Support Grants</div>

<div class="container">

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  A limited number of Student Support Grants are available for students attending iSES {{ site.year }},
  subject to the availability of funds.
</p>

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  Shortlisted candidates will be notified and must register for the conference by paying the eligible
  registration fee (student fee for RDS/SRF, full fee for paper if presenting, delegate fee if co-author).
  Participants with partial funding from their respective organizations will be given preference.
</p>

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  <strong>Attendance Requirement:</strong>
  To be eligible for the Student Support Grant, 100% active participation in all tutorial sessions,
  conference keynotes, plenary talks, and technical sessions of iSES {{ site.year }} is mandatory.
</p>

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  <strong>Accommodation Support:</strong>
  Students applying for accommodation support must stay at the NIT Goa hostel to qualify
  for the Student Accommodation Grant.
</p>

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  <strong>Travel Support:</strong>
  The Student Travel Grant covers 3rd AC train fare or actual travel expenses,
  whichever is lower, subject to submission of valid proof of travel.
</p>

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  Applicants must indicate the specific type of support required:
  <strong>Travel, Accommodation, or Both</strong>.
  This will help us extend support to a larger number of participants.
</p>

<p class="inline-7d27179924">
  <strong>Important:</strong>
  Submission of a Student Support Grant application does not guarantee approval or
  sanction of the grant. All grants are subject to the availability of funds and
  fulfillment of the eligibility requirements.
</p>

